## Realize it as a Dockerfile

Author a Dockerfile installing the selected libc/loader pair and preserving
interpreter, arch, permissions, and any hardening the writeup describes, served
over the declared protocol. Make only the choices the writeup backs; record
every unbacked assumption as such.

## Prefer an honest blocker

If the writeup gives no concrete runtime clue — no version, no libc, no offset —
do not guess. Emit `status: blocked` with a `runtime_inference_unsupported`
blocker quoting the writeup's silence; set `next_action` to supply a libc/loader
pair or an exploit that would anchor the runtime.

